# mydumper adds the dashes itself (case 3 of the rule).
-- options --
mydumper-version: v0.19.3-3
-- input.cnf --
[mydumper]
--threads=4
-- fixed-unsafe.cnf --
[mydumper]
threads=4
-- diagnostics --
2:1-2:10 error MDL401[unknown-option] `--threads` is not a mydumper option in v0.19.3-3: write `threads` without the dashes: mydumper adds `--` itself
  = mydumper aborts at startup: "option parsing failed: Unknown option ----threads, try --help".
  fix (unsafe): Rename the key to `threads`
